\section{Conclusion}
The Carrot-Collatz framework confirms that geometric physical principles can successfully redefine parity rules for rational dynamical systems. Through systematic profile variations (Versions 0--4), we demonstrated how physical cut definitions can drive trajectories toward infinity, force bounded decay funneling, or induce cross-boundary state oscillations. 

Crucially, our empirical investigation in Section 5 revealed an intriguing structural phenomenon within Version 4: while visually resembling unconstrained chaotic bouncing, its underlying dynamics are governed by a rigid, unbreakable 2-step parity period. Rather than behaving as an unconstrained pseudo-random stream, Version 4 operates as a perfectly balanced anti-persistent dual-phase oscillator—alternating strictly between an expansionary phase ($N > D$) and a reciprocal contraction phase ($N \ll D$). Future studies will focus on analyzing continuous floating-point entropy maps ($\ln N_t \pmod 1$) to extract chaotic magnitude dynamics independent of this internal state clock.

